     Factor scores are either incorrect or indeterminate (that is, partly arbitrary). How indeterminate depends (primarily) on how many indicators and how strong the loadings. By contrast, the factor mean parameter estimates are the estimates most consistent with the means of the observed variables, given the constraints in the model and your supporting assumptions. If you trust the model, then trust the parameter estimates that come from the model.

