Hi,

> I expect many indirect effects. Is it possible to estimate direct/indirect/total effect via path analysis using sem (lavaan package)?

Yes! The tutorial page from lavaan (https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/mediation.html) has some useful information.

> How to input the fixed/random effects parameters?

I assume you are interested in multilevel mediation? In that case, you can perform multilevel mediation using the MSEM framework (see https://doi.org/10.1037/a0020141 <https://psycnet.apa.org/doi/10.1037/a0020141> or perhaps https://doi.org/10.1080/00273171.2018.1527676, although the latter specifically looks at the 1-1-1 setting). If you would choose to work with MSEM using lavaan, then it is important to know that random slopes are currently not available in lavaan.

Hope this helps! (Perhaps someone with more experience in the field will also respond and give you more(/better) advice.)

Best wishes,

Jasper

